## Why This Is Asked
Advanced latency management in multi-tenant clusters requires concrete CRD-driven control with observable outcomes and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes CRD and controller reconciliation loops
- Prometheus-based latency metrics (p95) and windowing
- Mitigations: HPA scaling, admission throttling, proxy-sidecar rate limits
- Status, events, auditability, and rollback semantics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: reconciliation skeleton
function reconcile(spec, status) {
  const latency = queryPrometheus(spec.namespace, spec.serviceSelector, 'p95');
  if (latency > spec.budgetMs) {
    scaleOut(spec.namespace, spec.serviceSelector);
    enableRateLimit(spec.sidecarSvc, spec.budgetMs);
  } else {
    removeRateLimit(spec.sidecarSvc);
  }
  return { observedLatency: latency, breached: latency > spec.budgetMs };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test canary deployments for this policy?
- What safety checks would you implement to avoid flapping or service disruption?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant GPU sharing in Kubernetes, MIG partition management, NVIDIA device plugin integration, and the ability to build custom resource controllers for quota enforcement with burst handling.

## Key Concepts

- GPU quota management in shared clusters
- MIG (Multi-Instance GPU) partitions
- CRD and controller patterns
- Resource enforcement via scheduler hints
- Observability for GPU workloads

## Code Example

```go
func (r *GPUQuotaReconciler) Reconcile(ctx context.Context, req ctrl.Request) (ctrl.Result, error) {
    ns := &corev1.Namespace{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, ns); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    gpuQuota := &GPUQuota{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, gpuQuota); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    available GPUs, err := r.getAvailableGPUs(ns.Name)
    if err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, err
    }

    if gpuQuota.Spec.Burst.Enabled {
        if isWithinBurstWindow(gpuQuota) {
            return r.reconcileBurst(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
        }
    }

    return r.enforceQuota(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
}
```
